# Compile with MiKTeX

This machine has MiKTeX installed. Use it whenever the paper needs compiling. Do not skip compilation because `pdflatex` is missing from `PATH`.

- Engines:
  - `C:\Users\guill\AppData\Local\Programs\MiKTeX\miktex\bin\x64\pdflatex.exe`
  - `C:\Users\guill\AppData\Local\Programs\MiKTeX\miktex\bin\x64\bibtex.exe`
- Working directory: `paper/`
- Bibliography: `bibliography.bib` + `aasjournalv7.bst` (AASTeX v7). After bib changes run `bibtex shs_roman`.
- Command: `pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode shs_roman.tex` (run twice for cross-references; if the `.bbl` is stale, `pdflatex` → `bibtex` → `pdflatex` ×2)
- After editing `paper/shs_roman.tex` or regenerating `paper/f1.pdf` / `paper/f2.pdf`, recompile
